 Local Ethereum dev network with Hardhat
1. Install prerequisites (once)
In PowerShell:

powershell

winget install OpenJS.NodeJS.LTS
Close/reopen the terminal, then check:

powershell

node -### 2. Create a project and local chain

 PowerShell**, from `C:\Users\USER`:

```bash
mkdir my-blockchain && cd my-blockchain

npm init -y
npm install --save-dev hardhat

npx hardhat
`` choose:

- “Create a JavaScript project”
- Accept defaults

Hardhat creates a sample project.

### 3. Run the local blockchain node

In the same directory:

```bash
npx hardhat node
This:

Starts a local Ethereum JSON-RPC node at `http://127.0.0.1:8545 test accounts with private keys and test ETH
Leave this terminal running.

4. Deploy a contract to your local network
Open a second terminal, go to the same folder:

bash

cd C:/Users/USER/my-blockchain
npx hardhat run scripts/deploy.js --network localhost
This uses the sample contract and deploy script Hardhat generated.

Now you have:

A running local blockchain
A deployed smart contract
RPC endpoint at http://127.0.0:8545 you can connect to from web apps or scripts
